    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog centers on leveraging high-ceiling matchups against soft pitching rotations, with **Taylor Ward** (70.17) and **Lawrence Butler** (69.28) emerging as our premier plays. **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Rea, while **Lawrence Butler** is poised to capitalize on his elite dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) against Melton. We are also looking for a breakout performance from **Dylan Beavers** (68.38); despite the caution surrounding his matchup against an elite defensive catcher, the combination of favorable park factors and platoon splits keeps his efficiency high. **Cal Raleigh** (66.37) rounds out our top-tier targets, as his #4 spot in the order and the ability to leverage Phillips' xERA of 4.78 provide significant value in the power categories.\n\nOur bench strategy was dictated by efficiency thresholds, with **Jung Hoo Lee** (42.41) serving as the most difficult exclusion of the day. While **Jung Hoo Lee** saw a bump from his dynamic platoon edge, he ultimately could not overcome the negative drag of facing an elite arm like Cease. Similar logic applied to **Masyn Winn**, who, despite the prime #1 lineup spot, suffered from a -19% SP skill penalty that suppressed his score to 41.31. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Tyler Freeman**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, and **Gavin Sheets**; while their projected scores are solid, these \"Lineup Pending\" designations introduce variance. Furthermore, **Bryce Harper** (56.59) remains a mandatory start for his high-end xwOBA, even though he faces a stiff test in Burns, and **Luis Arraez** (44.64) is currently our riskiest active asset given his poor matchup against Cease. Be wary of **Zack Gelof** (58.18); while his #1 spot is encouraging, the potential for a low-SB game against an elite defensive backstop creates a narrow margin for error.",
